# interplay_memlive_migration_drops_range: A suspend, and a resume on a fresh device (a migration) whose memory map lists only the first RAM range: task 1, in the first range, has a shared buffer whose page is in the second (8 GiB) range, used before. rvg_device_did_resume rebuilds the task from its root word, and the buffer, made again at its next use, finds its guest page in no range of the new map and faults, while a buffer in the first range works. The map and isolate setups only: the blocks setup has no memory map (its host calls map guest RAM through callbacks). The memory map is fixed at device creation (RvgDeviceConfig.memory_map, copied at rvg_device_create; QEMU builds it once, apple-gfx.c:505-513), so only a migration can drop a range.
